# Repository Engineering Directives

- Break complex tasks into small, ordered steps; keep simple work direct.
- Inspect relevant code first and preserve unrelated user changes.
- Make precise, targeted edits instead of rewriting intact modules.
- Deliver complete, runnable code with no placeholder implementations or filler.
- Prefer the simplest sufficient solution; avoid unnecessary dependencies,
  wrappers, abstractions, and bloated files.
- Run relevant checks after changes, fix issues caused by the work, and never
  claim a check passed unless it was actually run.
- Audit changes for logic bugs, edge cases, security risks, type safety,
  regressions, and missing validation before completion.
- Build UI with semantic structure, responsive behavior, keyboard access,
  visible focus states, accessible labels, sufficient contrast, and appropriate
  reduced-motion support.
- Follow higher-priority platform and user instructions if they conflict with
  this file.

